# CLAUDE.md uses git's DEFAULT text merge -- deliberately NOT merge=union.
#
# union was here because CLAUDE.md only ever grew: two branches each appending
# a bullet merged without a conflict. That stops being true the moment a change
# RESTRUCTURES the file, because union never deletes. It resolves delete-vs-edit
# by keeping BOTH sides, silently, with no conflict markers -- so a branch that
# moves a section out to docs/ has that section resurrected by any merge from a
# branch that also touched the file, leaving two copies and no signal.
#
# Not hypothetical: an auto-resolve merge did exactly that to the companion
# repo's extraction, doubling a list back to 48k characters while reporting a
# clean merge. This file is now an index with pointers into docs/, so the same
# delete-heavy merges will happen here.
#
# With the default driver those merges conflict, loudly, and a human resolves.
